########################################################################
#
# .gitignore DIME template
# https://github.com/worldbank/DIMEwiki/tree/master/Topics/GitHub
#
# We recommend that you create a .gitignore file using GitHub's tools and
# replace the content of that file with the content of this file. Otherwise
# you have to rename this file .gitignore. But if you rename the fine in a
# regular folder window PCs and Macs are likely to keep the file extension
# so that the file ends up being names .gitignore.txt. Code editors like, Atom,
# can edit the file extension, but if you are not familiar with how to do that,
# we recommend that you generate an ignore file using GitHub and simply replace
# the content of that file.
#
# Note that if you are using GitKraken you need to use version 5.x or more
# recent for this template to work properly
#
########################################################################

#######################
# Start by ignoring everything, and below we are explicitly saying
# what to not ignore
*

#######################
# List of files with GitHub functionality anywhere in the repo
# that we do not want to ignore

# These files include GitHub settings
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!/.github/**

# Keep markdown files used for documentation on GitHub
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!LICENSE.md
!LICENSE
# VERSION is extensionless, so the deny-all above hides it without this rule
!VERSION

# r/.Rbuildignore is extensionless too, so the deny-all hides it. It has to be
# tracked or the fix it encodes does not ship: without it `R CMD build` sweeps whatever
# a sibling toolchain left in r/ into the tarball, and `R CMD check --as-cran` found 7
# .pytest_cache entries inside the built package. Caught only because the file failed to
# appear in `git status` after being written -- the same allowlist trap that once
# published the net site without stata.toc.
!r/.Rbuildignore

#######################
# For performance reasons, if a folder is already ignored, then
# GitHub does not check the content for that folder for matches
# with additional rules. The line below includes folder in the
# top folder (but not their content), so that anything matching
# the rules below will still not be ignored.
!*/

#######################
# The following file types are code that should always be
# included no matter where in the repository folder they are
# located unless you explicitly ignore that folder

# Stata
!/**/*.do
!/**/*.ado
!/**/*.sthlp

# The Stata net-site manifests. The deny-all above hides them and neither *.ado nor
# *.sthlp covers them, so in THIS repository they survived only by having been
# tracked before the deny-all existed -- git skips .gitignore for files already in
# the index. Any fresh export drops them, which is exactly what happened when the
# public distribution repository was first built: it came out without the two files
# that MAKE it a Stata net site, and -net install- from the documented public URL
# returned 404. Verify with: git ls-files | git check-ignore --no-index --stdin
!/stata/stata.toc
!/stata/datalib.pkg

# R-scrips and Rmarkdown-scripts
!/**/*.R
!/**/*.rds
!/**/*.Rmd

# LaTeX
!/**/*.tex

# Python
!/**/*.py
!/**/*.ipynb

# PowerShell
!/**/*.ps1

# Matlab
!/**/*.m

# Markdown
!/**/*.md

# Tableau Dataviz
!/**/*.twb

# Dyntext script
!docs/001_data/dyntext*.txt
!docs/001_data/*.html

# csv files in input folders
!/**/*_rawdata/*.csv
!/data/hosted_in_repo/*.csv
!/**/*_rawdata/*/*.csv

# Contract + conformance kit
!/config/*.yml
!/tests/**/*.csv
!/tests/**/*.yml
!/tests/fixtures/**/*.dta
!/tests/**/*.json
!/**/.gitkeep

# R package (r/)
!/r/DESCRIPTION
!/r/NAMESPACE
!/r/LICENSE
!/r/inst/*.yml
!/r/man/*.Rd

# Python package (python/)
!/python/pyproject.toml
!/python/.gitignore
!/python/src/datalib/py.typed
!/python/src/datalib/*.yml
#/02_benchmarking/023_results/*.csv
#/01_data/012_programs/*/*.csv


# csv files in selected input folders
!08_2pager/081_data/cleaned_*.csv
!08_2pager/081_data/hosted_in_repo/*.csv
!05_working_paper/053_outputs/*correlations.csv
!02_simulation/023_outputs/*.csv
!02_simulation/023_outputs/*/*.csv

# excel for working paper
!05_working_paper/051_rawdata/LPV_*Template.xlsx
!05_working_paper/053_outputs/LPV_*PAPER.xlsx

##################
#Include images used in the 2pager template
!08_2pager/082_program/Rmd_template/Rmd_template_images/*.png

#Include ppt template in the slides folder
!10_slides/102_program/Rmd_template/*.pptx

#Include the Excel input file
#!08_2pager/081_data/twopager_input.xls

#Include the Excel input file with Name of TTLs
!08_2pager/081_data/hosted_in_repo/20190903_TTL List.xlsx

#Do not commit the intermediate tex files generated by the Rmd
08_2pager/083_interm_output/raw_output_2pagers/*.tex

#Commit the pdf output and png
!08_2pager/083_interm_output/raw_output_2pagers/demo_twopager.pdf
!08_2pager/083_interm_output/graphs/_*.png

#Do not commit the aggregation tex files
#08_2pager/084_2pagers/*/*.tex
#08_2pager/084_2pagers/*/*/*.tex

# image files in documentation folders
!/docs/*/*/*.png
!/docs/*/*/*.jpg
!/docs/*/*.png
!/docs/*/*.jpg
!/docs/*.png
!/docs/*.jpg
!/docs/*.zip

# PPTX in documentation folders
!/docs/*.pptx

# PDFs files in documentation folder
!/docs/pdf/*.pdf


#######################
# Include all the files with passwords or tokens here. All files named
# password or passwords are with this template ignored no matter which
# format you are using. Additionally, all content in any folder called
password or passwords are also ignored. NOTE that your project might be
using different names and then you must edit the lines below accordingly.
password.*
passwords.*
password/
passwords/
.Rproj.user

temp
*.tex
10_slides/102_program/1020_data_cleaning.R
tempCodeRunnerFile.do
*/tempCodeRunnerFile.do
*/**/temp*.do
*/**/**/temp*.do
# Built by scripts/sync-public.ps1 outside the repo; the LICENSE variant it ships
# is tracked in dist-public/ but the built tree never lives here.
